# Browser captures. A HAR records the FULL request — Cookie and Authorization
# headers, session ids, anything the browser sent. This repository is public,
# so a HAR must never land in it, not even briefly: git history is forever and
# a force-push does not un-leak a credential.
#
# To pull the APMI payload out of a capture WITHOUT the headers, extract only
# the response body (see scripts/apmi-request-notes.md):
#   jq -r '[.log.entries[] | select(.request.url|test("loadIAReport";"i"))][0].response.content.text' \
#     ~/Downloads/www.apmiindia.org.har > scripts/apmi-report.json
*.har
*.harfile

# Saved APMI payloads. Public performance data rather than a secret, but it
# comes out of a browser session — eyeball one before you ever force-add it.
scripts/apmi-report*.json
scripts/pms-data*.csv
